# SoulSearch Architecture Cleanup Plan

Source analysis: `docs/cleanup-report.md`
Parent work item: `Cleanup code architecture` in `docs/project.todo`

This file is the authoritative implementation checklist for the architecture
cleanup. Update items as work lands; do not mark a phase complete because nearby
coverage exists or because the code compiles.

Status legend:

- ☐ pending
- ◐ in progress
- ✔ complete (append `@done(YY-MM-DD HH:MM)`)
- ✘ cancelled (append `@cancelled(YY-MM-DD HH:MM)` and a reason)

## Behavior-preservation constraints

These are invariants for every phase, not optional design goals:

- Search filters remain ordered relevance criteria; partial matches stay in the
  results instead of becoming hard exclusions.
- Result ordering remains: matched criterion count, weighted score, raw score,
  resident name, then unit ID.
- Attribute, trait, and skill baseline/scoring rules do not change as part of
  architecture cleanup.
- Existing colors, CP437 symbols, label widths, and `FILTER_ACTION_WIDTH = 3`
  mouse action zones remain exact unless handled as a separately approved UI
  change.
- Results-list keyboard navigation and focus behavior remain unchanged.
- Filter order and high/low directions continue to survive closing and reopening
  the window within the current supported lifetime.
- Position remains a live read when zooming; it must not be added back to the
  resident snapshot.
- Window dragging, resizing, dropdown visibility, tooltips, stats sorting,
  refresh, zoom, and close behavior remain functional.
- LuaLS annotations remain accurate as functions and types move between modules.
- `tools/Build.ps1` must pass at every phase boundary. In-game behavior is not
  considered verified by the syntax check alone.

