## Phase 2 - Search API and result model cleanup

Depends on: Phase 1.

Goal: reduce search to one input contract and an explicitly tested result
ordering/model.

Status: in progress — implementation, automated validation, and a fresh-script
live DFHack probe are complete; visual result/filter comparison remains pending
with the interactive smoke run.

Canonical input policy: filters are ordered `{id, direction}` entries. Unknown
IDs, malformed entries, and directions other than `high`/`low` are ignored. The
first valid occurrence of a duplicate ID wins and retains its priority.

### Canonical search input

✔ Confirm that no external script consumes the private alternatives
  `selected_descriptors` or `selected_filter_ids`. @done(26-07-10 07:20)
✔ Choose ordered `{id, direction}` filters as the canonical `search.apply()`
  input. @done(26-07-10 07:20)
✔ Normalize and validate filter entries once at the API boundary through the
  descriptor catalog. @done(26-07-10 07:20)
✔ Define behavior for unknown IDs, duplicate IDs, and invalid directions.
  @done(26-07-10 07:20)
✔ Remove unused compatibility input paths when confirmed private.
  @done(26-07-10 07:20)
✘ If a compatibility path must remain, isolate it in one named adapter and
  document its precedence instead of branching inside `apply()`.
  @cancelled(26-07-10 07:20) No compatibility path or external consumer remains.

### Search internals

✔ Extract the result ordering function into a named comparator.
  @done(26-07-10 07:20)
✔ Add direct comparator tests for every tie-break level.
  @done(26-07-10 07:20)
✔ Keep scoring/evaluation separate from result presentation formatting.
  @done(26-07-10 07:20)
✔ Avoid copying immutable descriptor tables; copy only selected-filter state
  that is actually mutable. @done(26-07-10 07:20)
✔ Rename any remaining shallow-copy helper so its behavior is explicit.
  @done(26-07-10 07:20) The obsolete shallow-copy helper was removed entirely.

### Result model

✔ Audit every `SoulSearchResult` field against production consumers.
  @done(26-07-10 07:20)
✔ Remove unused `matched_criteria`, `criteria_count`, and `match_label` fields
  if no consumer is found. @done(26-07-10 07:20)
✔ Keep `filter_criteria`, `matched_count`, and score fields only where required
  by presentation or sorting. @done(26-07-10 07:20)
✔ Update LuaLS result annotations to match the final shape.
  @done(26-07-10 07:20)
✔ Update fixtures to build/compare the final result contract.
  @done(26-07-10 07:20)

### Phase 2 exit gate

✔ `search.apply()` exposes one documented input shape. @done(26-07-10 07:20)
✔ Result objects contain no unowned compatibility or presentation fields.
