## Phase 3 - Filter state model and persistence boundary

Depends on: Phases 0-2.

Goal: remove filter collection rules and persistence from
`SoulSearchWindow`, using one canonical state representation.

### Pure filter state model

☐ Create `internal/soulsearch/filter_state.lua` with LuaLS types.
☐ Represent active filters as one ordered collection of `{id, direction}`.
☐ Add an ID index only if needed for clear invariants or measured lookup cost.
☐ Implement atomic `add`, `remove`, `clear`, `set_direction`, and `move`
  transitions.
☐ Implement descriptor-catalog validation for stale IDs and invalid directions.
☐ Define and test duplicate-add behavior.
☐ Define and test move behavior at the first/last boundary.
☐ Make each operation report whether the state actually changed.
☐ Ensure returned/read state cannot be mutated accidentally by a caller.

### State tests

☐ Add table-driven add/remove/clear tests.
☐ Add direction-change tests for active and inactive filters.
☐ Add priority reorder and boundary tests.
☐ Add validation tests for stale, duplicate, and malformed entries.
☐ Add copy/isolation tests proving saved state does not alias live state.
☐ Add ordered serialization tests for the search input.

### Persistence boundary

☐ Add explicit `load()` and `save(state)` operations for session persistence.
☐ Preserve the current persistence lifetime unless a separate behavior change
  is approved.
☐ Move `saved_filter_modes` and `saved_filter_order` out of `ui.lua`.
☐ Validate persisted state against the active descriptor catalog on load.
☐ Document the owner responsible for clearing or retaining state on script/world
  lifecycle changes.

### Window migration

☐ Replace `selected_filter_modes`, `selected_filter_order`, and derived
  `selected_filters` with the canonical filter state.
☐ Migrate add, remove, clear, direction, and priority methods one at a time.
☐ Remove window methods that only implement collection lookup/copy/validation.
☐ Ensure setting direction on a new filter performs one atomic state change,
  not an add refresh followed by a direction refresh.
☐ Keep widget construction and geometry unchanged during this phase.

### Phase 3 exit gate

☐ The window no longer owns filter collection mutation or persistence rules.
☐ One logical state action results in one state transition.
☐ Filter-state and search characterization tests pass.
☐ `tools/Build.ps1` and `tools/Test.ps1` pass.
☐ In-game add/remove/clear/reorder/direction and reopen persistence match the
  baseline.

## Phase 4 - UI orchestration and invalidation paths

Depends on: Phase 3.

Goal: replace scattered/nested update cascades with explicit view update paths
while preserving the existing widget tree.

### Update ownership

☐ Inventory which views depend on filter state, picker query, picker visibility,
  resident rows, name query, result selection, and stats sort state.
☐ Add one narrow refresh method for active filter choices.
☐ Add one narrow refresh method for picker choices.
☐ Add one narrow result recomputation method.
☐ Add one narrow stats refresh method.
☐ Ensure refresh methods update derived views only and do not mutate domain
  state.
☐ Ensure state-transition methods do not call other state-transition methods.

### Event flow

☐ Route each filter-state change through one controller callback/update pass.
☐ Remove repeated `update_available_filter_choices()` and
  `update_available_skill_choices()` call sequences from individual actions.
☐ Separate picker open/close changes from filter-data changes.
☐ Ensure opening or closing a picker does not recompute resident results.
☐ Preserve selected filter index after direction/reorder changes where valid.
☐ Preserve selected resident by unit ID across result recomputation where the
  resident remains present.
☐ Define the fallback selection when the previous resident disappears.
☐ Ensure name-query changes recompute results once.
☐ Ensure resident refresh recomputes results once after collection completes.

### Input and focus regression checks

☐ Verify mouse filter actions still select the row before applying the action.
☐ Verify up/down and fast up/down keys continue controlling the results list.
☐ Verify filter-priority hotkeys still operate on the selected filter.
☐ Verify Backspace closes an open picker before reaching parent handling.
☐ Verify Enter and zoom hotkey behavior remains unchanged.

### Phase 4 exit gate

☐ Every user action has one documented state/update path.
☐ No view refresh is nested inside a domain-state transition.
☐ Instrumentation or focused tests show one result recomputation per logical
  action.
☐ `tools/Build.ps1` and `tools/Test.ps1` pass.
☐ The full in-game interaction smoke checklist passes with unchanged geometry.

