## Phase 6 - DFHack adapters, diagnostics, caches, and module lifecycle

Depends on: Phase 0. Prefer after Phase 5 so UI/core ownership is stable.

Goal: isolate external DFHack reads, make failures diagnosable, and define
cache/reload lifetime without changing user-facing fallbacks.

### Resident data adapter

☐ Identify the minimum DFHack reads needed for resident eligibility, names,
  profession, traits, physical attributes, mental attributes, skills, and live
  position.
☐ Move defensive API calls behind narrowly named adapter functions.
☐ Keep resident row construction as pure table transformation where practical.
☐ Preserve graceful omission/fallback when optional reads fail.
☐ Add development diagnostics that aggregate or report failed reads once per
  API/field rather than spamming per resident.
☐ Keep diagnostics disabled or quiet in normal use.
☐ Add adapter/row fixture tests for residents with no soul, no personality,
  missing attributes, missing translations, and unknown skills.

### Behavior-rule verification

☐ Verify the skill progress formula against the supported DF/DFHack version
  before refactoring its implementation.
☐ Verify raw `PHYS_ATT_RANGE` and `MENT_ATT_RANGE` parsing against supported
  creature raw structure before changing the parser.
☐ Record the evidence used for both rules in code comments or test fixtures.
☐ Treat any formula/parser behavior change as separate from architecture cleanup
  and update expected behavior explicitly if approved.

### Cache lifetime

☐ Document the lifetime and owner of race median, skill-name, and descriptor
  caches.
☐ Add explicit cache reset functions where world/script lifecycle requires them.
☐ Ensure cache resets cannot occur in the middle of a search/update pass.
☐ Add tests proving cache reuse and explicit reset behavior.

### Script loading/reloading

☐ Decide whether the entrypoint's helper validates module contracts, reloads
  edited development scripts, or offers separate operations for each.
☐ Replace the nonexistent required `search` field check with the real `apply`
  contract if validation is the intent.
☐ If hot reload is intended, use one explicit DFHack-supported reload path for
  every internal module instead of forcing fallback for only `search.lua`.
☐ Define dependency reload order so `ui`, `search`, `attributes`, and shared
  modules do not retain mixed generations.
☐ Add an in-game development check proving an edited internal module is either
  consistently reloaded or consistently retained according to the contract.

### Phase 6 exit gate

☐ Resident transformation is testable with fixture/adapted data.
☐ Normal users retain graceful fallbacks and development failures are
  diagnosable.
☐ Cache invalidation and module reload ownership are documented and tested.
☐ `tools/Build.ps1` and `tools/Test.ps1` pass.
☐ In-game resident collection, refresh, name display, and zoom match baseline.

