## Phase 8 - Final validation and checklist closure

Depends on: all previous phases.

Goal: verify the complete architecture cleanup against both automated and
in-game evidence before closing the parent work item.

### Automated validation

☐ Run `tools/Build.ps1` from a clean shell.
☐ Run `tools/Test.ps1` from a clean shell.
☐ Run package creation and package-structure verification.
☐ Run whitespace/diff validation and resolve new warnings.
☐ Confirm test fixtures cover all ranking precedence levels and all filter-state
  transitions named in this plan.
☐ Confirm no test is marked skipped/expected-failure without a tracked reason.

### Architecture audit

☐ Confirm descriptors and skill taxonomy have one source of truth.
☐ Confirm descriptor lookup is indexed and searches do not rebuild metadata.
☐ Confirm filter state is independent of `SoulSearchWindow`.
☐ Confirm one user action causes at most one controlled result recomputation.
☐ Confirm search exposes one canonical filter input contract.
☐ Confirm result objects contain only fields with known consumers.
☐ Confirm `SoulSearchWindow` is a composition/event coordination layer.
☐ Confirm layout and hitbox metadata have one source of truth.
☐ Confirm DFHack reads, caches, and module reload lifecycle have explicit owners.

### Full in-game regression pass

☐ Open SoulSearch in fortress mode and verify invalid-mode messaging elsewhere.
☐ Verify resident names, professions, traits, attributes, skills, and relevance
  values with representative residents.
☐ Verify name query, no filters, one filter, multiple ordered filters, partial
  matches, high/low direction, and tied results.
☐ Verify add/remove/clear/reorder controls via keyboard and mouse.
☐ Verify every filter action's left/right x boundary.
☐ Verify attribute and skill picker search, category order, close behavior, and
  empty state.
☐ Verify results-list focus, normal/fast navigation, submit, and selection
  preservation after updates.
☐ Verify Stats panel headings, selected-filter table, category colors, values,
